This repository is a derivative work of the above.  It keeps the USB-boot /
rooting tooling (boot/), the tuner and descrambler sources (src/, include/) and
the Android housekeeping scripts (scripts/crash_guard.sh,
scripts/stop_android_tv.sh, scripts/smb400-tuner.sh) essentially unchanged, and
replaces the Mirakurun-BS4K layer (Alpine chroot + Node.js) with mirakc.

Changes made to the derived files:

  * scripts/smb400-tuner.sh
    GR path: pass portId as decimal 32 instead of "0x20".  tuner-stream-ng
    parses the argument with atoi(), so "0x20" evaluated to 0 and
    DMX_AttachTSPort(dmx=0, port=0) failed with 0x80150002, which broke ISDB-T
    reception entirely.

  * boot/initramfs_overlay/init.pixboot.rc
    The `mirakurun_proxy` service is replaced by a `mirakc` service that runs
    /data/local/tmp/start_mirakc.sh.  The Alpine rootfs mkdir lines are removed
    (no chroot is used).  tuner_reaper.sh is added to the post-fs-data copies.

  * boot/build_initramfs.sh
    Overlay file list updated to match the above.

Removed from the original because they are Mirakurun-specific:
scripts/setup_proot.sh, scripts/start_mirakurun.sh,
patches/node-rs-crc32-index.js, config/{server,tuners,channels}.yml.

---

Third-party binaries redistributed in bin/:

  * mirakc — https://github.com/mirakc/mirakc (MIT)
    Built from a fork with per-channel-type filter/job overrides
    (`filters.for-channel-types`), required for the BS4K remux.

  * mirakc-arib — https://github.com/mirakc/mirakc-arib (MIT / see project)
    Taken from the official mirakc/tools:alpine armv7 image.

  * dantto4k — https://github.com/nekohkr/dantto4k
    Built for armv7 with the portability patch in tools/dantto4k/.
    Links TSDuck (https://tsduck.io/, BSD-2-Clause).
    The ACAS/AES-NI path is stubbed out in this build; it must be run with
    --frontend-descrambled.

  * tuner-stream-*, b21dec, b61dec — built from src/ in this repository
    (Apache-2.0, from pix-smb400-mirakurun).

See each upstream project for its full license text.
